\[
\binom{n}{r} = \frac{n!}{r!(n-r)!}
\]

Here, \( n = 14 \) and \( r = 6 \). Plugging these values into the formula, we get:

\[
\binom{14}{6} = \frac{14!}{6! \cdot 8!}
\]

First, we calculate the factorials:

\[
14! = 14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10 \times 9 \times 8!
\]

